      "text": "To find the value of \\(19^2 - 17^2 + 15^2 - 13^2 + 11^2 - 9^2 + 7^2 - 5^2 + 3^2 - 1^2\\), we can use properties of differences of squares. The difference of squares formula is \\(a^2 - b^2 = (a - b)(a + b)\\).\n\nFirst, let's pair the terms with opposite signs:\n\n1. \\(19^2 - 17^2 = (19 - 17)(19 + 17)\\)\n2. \\(15^2 - 13^2 = (15 - 13)(15 + 13)\\)\n3. \\(11^2 - 9^2 = (11 - 9)(11 + 9)\\)\n4. \\(7^2 - 5^2 = (7 - 5)(7 + 5)\\)\n5. \\(3^2 - 1^2 = (3 - 1)(3 + 1)\\)\n\nNow we can rewrite the original expression using these pairs:\n\n\\[19^2 - 17^2 + 15^2 - 13^2 + 11^2 - 9^2 + 7^2 - 5^2 + 3^2 - 1^2 = (19 - 17)(19 + 17) + (15 - 13)(15 + 13) + (11 - 9)(11 + 9) + (7 - 5)(7 + 5) + (3 - 1)(3 + 1) - (1 - 1)\\]\n\nThe expression simplifies because the last term has \\(1^2 = 1\\), which cancels out with the first term \\(-1^2 = -1\\):\n\n\\[= (2)(36) + (2)(28) + (2)(24) + (2)(12) + (2)(4) - 1\\]\n\nNext, we calculate each multiplication:\n\n\\[= 72 + 56 + 48 + 24 + 8 - 1\\]\n\nFinally, we sum these values:\n\n\\[= 208 - 1\\]\n\nSo the final answer is:\n\n\\[\\boxed{207}\\]\n```python\n# Define the terms to be squared and their respective complements\nterms = [19, 17], [15, 13], [11, 9], [7, 5], [3, 1]\n\n# Calculate the sums using the difference of squares property\ntotal_value = sum((a_i - b_i) * (a_i + b_i) for a_i, b_i in terms)\n\n# Include the last term which is (-1)^2\nfinal_value = total_value - 1\n\nprint(final_value)\n```",
